    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm having some trouble with an iam policy. i'm trying to let a lambda function write logs to a specific s3 bucket but i keep getting an access denied error. i thought i had the permissions right but it's still failing. can u take a look at this json and see what i'm missing?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-logs-bucket\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your policy is close, but you are missing the resource qualifier for the object path within the bucket. To allow writing to a *specific* bucket, you generally need to specify the object ARN format, which looks like `arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name/*`. Also, remember that logging often requires more than just `s3:PutObject`; check if your Lambda execution role also needs permissions for services like CloudWatch Logs destination. Ensure that the IAM role attached to your Lambda function is explicitly using this policy.",
