      "role": "user",
      "content": "ohhh ok that makes sense. i forgot the /* part. so i updated it to \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-logs-bucket/*\" and it still says access denied when the lambda tries to run. i checked the execution role and it definitely has the policy attached. is there anything else that could be blocking it? like maybe something on the bucket side itself?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, permissions on the S3 bucket itself are a very common blocker. Even with the Lambda policy updated, the S3 bucket policy might be explicitly denying access or might not allow cross-account access if the Lambda role is from a different account. Double-check the S3 bucket policy to ensure it doesn't contain a `Deny` statement overriding your IAM permission. Finally, verify that the Lambda's IAM role has the necessary `sts:AssumeRole` permissions if there's any complex role-chaining involved.",
